        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel's defence network challenged by Iranian cluster ballistic missiles Middle East Issued on: 25/03/2026 - 18:06 As the regional conflict between Israel and Iran enters a volatile new phase, a banned weapon of war is reappearing over civilian centres. While Israel’s defence systems remain robust, a new threat - the cluster ballistic missile - is testing the limits of safety. Unlike a single warhead, these missiles release hundreds of \"bomblets,\" turning neighbourhoods into active minefields long after the sirens stop. Heritage sites in the Middle East under threat due to conflict 25/03/2026 Middle East Iran 'dismisses' US 15-point peace plan, issues its own ceasefire proposal 25/03/2026 Middle East Once seeking de-escalation, Saudi Arabia now sees ‘no coexistence’ with hardline Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East US goals shift: 'At the beginning of the Iran war, the US and Israel were on the same page' 25/03/2026 Middle East US demands of 15-point peace plan likely 'unacceptable' for Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East Unclear 'how much of a negotiation is taking place' between US and Iran 25/03/2026 Middle East What do we know of the US's 15-point peace plan sent to Iran? 25/03/2026 Middle East Inside the Palestinian camp in Beirut where residents are staying put, for now 25/03/2026 Middle East In Lebanon, some schools choose to stay open despite the war 25/03/2026 Middle East"
